course: dictionary
lesson: 13092
title: Spelling with your hands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have no sign of their own, and names are often like that. To say them, you can fingerspell: spell the word out letter by letter, using a hand shape for each letter. «My name is Amara, so I fingerspell A-M-A-R-A.» Each hand shape stands for one letter of the alphabet.
explain: Fingerspelling is part of many sign languages, such as British Sign Language (BSL) and American Sign Language (ASL). They use the same idea but different hand shapes, so a letter in ASL may look different from the same letter in BSL. «Ben fingerspelt his name slowly so his friend could follow.» Slow, clear hands help the other person read each letter.
explain: Practice makes fingerspelling quicker. Start by learning the alphabet hand shapes one letter at a time. Then try short words you see every day, like cat or dog, before you try longer names.
fact: To fingerspell is to spell out a word letter by letter using hand shapes.
fact: People fingerspell names and words that have no sign.
fact: BSL uses two hands for fingerspelling, and ASL uses one.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «fingerspell your name» and «the fingerspelling alphabet».
fact: Fingerspelling is only one part of sign language; many signs stand for whole words or ideas.
exercise: What does fingerspelling mean? | To say a word out loud | To sing a song with your hands | *To spell a word letter by letter with hand shapes | To draw a picture of a word
exercise: «Maya fingerspells her name in BSL.» How many hands does BSL use for fingerspelling? | None | One | *Two | Three
exercise: Why do people fingerspell a name? | Because hands get tired of signing | Because it is a secret code | *Because the name has no sign of its own | Because names are always longer than other words
test: «Sam fingerspelt his name using one hand, the way ASL does.» Which sign language uses one hand for fingerspelling? | Neither uses fingerspelling | Both use two hands | British Sign Language | *American Sign Language
test: «The teacher asked Lily to fingerspell her name.» Which phrase means the same as this? | Sing your name | Whisper your name | *Spell your name with hand shapes | Draw your name
exam: Mia says fingerspell means to draw a word in the air. Is she right? | Yes, but only for names | Yes, it means drawing letters | *No, it means spelling a word letter by letter with hand shapes | No, it means to shout a word
